{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"wcf:31","provision":"WCF 31","book":"wcf","book_name":"Westminster Confession of Faith","abbreviation":"WCF","reference":"31","title":"Chapter 31 · Of Synods and Councils","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/wcf/31/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#wcf/31","current_text":{"html":"<section class=\"provision-chapter-section\" id=\"wcf-31.1\"><h3><a href=\"/pca-ga/provisions/wcf/31.1/\">WCF 31.1</a></h3><div class=\"provision-text\"><p>For the better government, and further edification of the church, there ought to be such assemblies as are commonly called synods or councils: and it belongeth to the overseers and other rulers of the particular churches, by virtue of their office, and the power which Christ hath given them for edification and not for destruction, to appoint such assemblies; and to convene together in them, as often as they shall judge it expedient for the good of the church.</p></div></section><section class=\"provision-chapter-section\" id=\"wcf-31.2\"><h3><a href=\"/pca-ga/provisions/wcf/31.2/\">WCF 31.2</a></h3><div class=\"provision-text\"><p>It belongeth to synods and councils, ministerially to determine controversies of faith, and cases of conscience; to set down rules and directions for the better ordering of the public worship of God, and government of his church; to receive complaints in cases of maladministration, and authoritatively to determine the same: which decrees and determinations, if consonant to the Word of God, are to be received with reverence and submission; not only for their agreement with the Word, but also for the power whereby they are made, as being an ordinance of God appointed thereunto in his Word.</p></div></section><section class=\"provision-chapter-section\" id=\"wcf-31.3\"><h3><a href=\"/pca-ga/provisions/wcf/31.3/\">WCF 31.3</a></h3><div class=\"provision-text\"><p>All synods or councils, since the Apostles' times, whether general or particular, may err; and many have erred. Therefore they are not to be made the rule of faith, or practice; but to be used as a help in both.</p></div></section><section class=\"provision-chapter-section\" id=\"wcf-31.4\"><h3><a href=\"/pca-ga/provisions/wcf/31.4/\">WCF 31.4</a></h3><div class=\"provision-text\"><p>Synods and councils are to handle, or conclude nothing, but that which is ecclesiastical: and are not to intermeddle with civil affairs which concern the commonwealth, unless by way of humble petition in cases extraordinary; or, by way of advice, for satisfaction of conscience, if they be thereunto required by the civil magistrate.</p></div></section>","text":"WCF 31.1For the better government, and further edification of the church, there ought to be such assemblies as are commonly called synods or councils: and it belongeth to the overseers and other rulers of the particular churches, by virtue of their office, and the power which Christ hath given them for edification and not for destruction, to appoint such assemblies; and to convene together in them, as often as they shall judge it expedient for the good of the church.WCF 31.2It belongeth to synods and councils, ministerially to determine controversies of faith, and cases of conscience; to set down rules and directions for the better ordering of the public worship of God, and government of his church; to receive complaints in cases of maladministration, and authoritatively to determine the same: which decrees and determinations, if consonant to the Word of God, are to be received with reverence and submission; not only for their agreement with the Word, but also for the power whereby they are made, as being an ordinance of God appointed thereunto in his Word.WCF 31.3All synods or councils, since the Apostles' times, whether general or particular, may err; and many have erred. Therefore they are not to be made the rule of faith, or practice; but to be used as a help in both.WCF 31.4Synods and councils are to handle, or conclude nothing, but that which is ecclesiastical: and are not to intermeddle with civil affairs which concern the commonwealth, unless by way of humble petition in cases extraordinary; or, by way of advice, for satisfaction of conscience, if they be thereunto required by the civil magistrate."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"f8bde72b35f9475713a5751081d525f119bc6b4daf3b43ddc86694065015654b","parent_id":null,"children":["wcf:31.1","wcf:31.2","wcf:31.3","wcf:31.4"],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"not_available"},"relationship_count":7,"relationships":[{"id":"wcf:31--case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Sears v. Nashville Presbytery","year":2025,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"wcf:31--case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.md:occ-1c6613ec6b05","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2023-18.md","locator":{},"excerpt